{"step": 0, "mode": "eval", "task_id": "nist-gcr-17-917-46v3:p64:c0:q4:abstain:1", "format": true, "correct": true, "terminated": true, "n_tokens": 7, "length": -0.0, "total": 1.0, "text": "Not in the provided passages."}
{"step": 0, "mode": "eval", "task_id": "nist-gcr-17-917-46v3:p64:c0:q4:abstain:1", "format": true, "correct": false, "terminated": true, "n_tokens": 130, "length": -0.0, "total": 0.1, "text": "Axial growth and lengthening effects due to flexure and curvature in restrained reinforced concrete members can be captured using empirical equations like those provided by Kwon (2016), which incorporate terms for the compressive axial load ratio, longitudinal tension-steel reinforcement ratio (ρT), and peak prior lateral drift ratio (DR) [nist-gcr-17-917-46v3:p47:c1]. These equations account for secant stiffness, effective flexural rigidity, and other deformation components [nist-gcr-17-917-46v3:p47:c1]."}
